# `push_batch_within`'s early exit, inverted to stop on the productive attempt.
#
# Real: stop at the first attempt that moves nothing, because a second attempt
# against an unchanged ring can only find the same answer. Inverted: stop at the
# first attempt that moves something.
#
# Against an ordinary iterator the two return the identical count, since
# single-threaded the first attempt takes everything the ring has room for, so
# the published total cannot see this and neither can the consumer's length.
# The detector's source yields one burst per attempt (see S7), so on a budget of
# three the real loop publishes three bursts and the inverted one publishes one.

id: S8
crate: ring_poll
file: src/lib.rs
round: 2026-10-01
round-failures: 1
detector: push_batch_within_spends_its_whole_budget_while_attempts_keep_moving_records

--- from
    if moved == 0 {
--- to
    if moved != 0 {   // PROBE ONLY — G12, was `==`
--- end
